§8§lPouncing Stalkers\n\n\
§0Spiders are remarkably quick creatures, though their exoskeletons are more fragile than their size might suggest. \
They appear to have sacrificed durability for speed, making them dangerous foes for—"
data modify storage bittersweet:almanac book.pages append value "\
—the ill-prepared. Their dark exterior allows them to camoflage in the dark. Combined with their long legs and ability to climb, \
they are very much cave predators. They often prey on bats, but aren't picky eaters."
data modify storage bittersweet:almanac book.pages append value "\
Upon pouncing on their prey, spiders will attempt to ensnare them with their webs."
